#define <<MODULE_UPPER>>_TIMEOUT_MS 100

/* internal state */
static bool initialized = false;
@

<<module:init>>=
int <<module_prefix>>_init(void) {
  if (initialized) return 0;
  /* TODO: hardware init: clocks, gpio, uart/i2c setup */
  initialized = true;
  return 0;
}
@

<<module:read>>=
int <<module_prefix>>_read(uint8_t *buf, unsigned len) {
  if (!initialized) return -3; /* not initialized */
  if (!buf || len < <<MODULE_UPPER>>_MIN_LEN) return -4; /* bad args */

  /* TODO: implement concrete read, e.g. polling or interrupt-driven */
  for (unsigned i = 0; i < len; ++i) {
    /* read byte into buf[i]; emulate blocking behaviour */
    buf[i] = 0; /* placeholder */
  }
  return 0;
}
@

<<module:shutdown>>=
void <<module_prefix>>_shutdown(void) {
  if (!initialized) return;
  /* TODO: power down hardware, disable clocks */
  initialized = false;
}
@

% -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% 6. Testing and validation
% -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

List test cases, expected results, and include the test harness code chunk.

Test cases:
1. init success -> expect return 0
2. read with insufficient buffer -> expect error -4
3. read after init -> expect 0 and valid data

<<test_harness.c>>=
#include "<<module_name>>.h"
#include <assert.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
  assert(<<module_prefix>>_init() == 0);
  uint8_t small[4];
  assert(<<module_prefix>>_read(small, sizeof(small)) == -4);

  uint8_t buf[16];
  int r = <<module_prefix>>_read(buf, sizeof(buf));
  printf("read returned %d\n", r);
  /* further asserts depend on implementation */
  <<module_prefix>>_shutdown();
  return 0;
}
@

% -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% 7. Build & tangling instructions
% -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Tangling (extract .c/.h):
- To extract source files: `notangle literate-doc-template.nw > tangled.c` or use named chunk extraction.
- To weave into TeX: `noweave literate-doc-template.nw > doc.tex` and then `pdflatex doc.tex`.

Recommended Makefile snippet (append to project Makefile):

<<Makefile.snip>>=
# Tangle step: generate implementation and examples
tangle:
	notangle literate-doc-template.nw > src/<<module_name>>.c
	notangle -index -noerrors -output=include/<<module_name>>.h literate-doc-template.nw

weave:
	noweave literate-doc-template.nw > docs/<<module_name>>.tex
	pdflatex -output-directory=docs docs/<<module_name>>.tex || true

.PHONY: tangle weave
@

% -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% 8. CI checklist & PR expectations
% -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

When opening a PR that changes implementation:
- Ensure the literate source is updated (not only the generated .c/.h)
- CI must run tangle -> build -> unit test (green)
- Include a brief changelog entry in the doc's "TODO / changelog" section

